WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.630
- Ah, well, Gloria's not
the only single parent

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:03.463
in the house.

00:00:03.463 --> 00:00:06.890
I am, and so as everyone in our audience,

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:07.830
I salute all of you.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:08.780
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.790
It's not an easy task,

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:12.980
and that's why this hour
we're gonna celebrate

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.819
what we pull off every day.

00:00:14.819 --> 00:00:16.860
I think we can all agree raising kids

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.410
in a two parent home is no easy task,

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:23.400
but doing it on your own requires
a special kind of strength

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.020
and patience and lots of prayer.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.160
Our first guest is also a single parent.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.170
She's the cohost of the
"Two Funny Mamas" podcast,

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:33.120
as well as a Weight Watchers ambassador.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.269
Give it up for our friend Kym Whitley

00:00:35.269 --> 00:00:40.269
(audience cheers)
(soft upbeat music)

00:00:55.225 --> 00:00:57.179
(audience applauding)

00:00:57.179 --> 00:00:59.061
Single parents in the audience.

00:00:59.061 --> 00:01:00.340
And you adopted as well.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:01.173
- I did.

00:01:01.173 --> 00:01:04.388
He was four days old
and it changed my life.

00:01:04.388 --> 00:01:06.490
And people always say, oh, you saved him,

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:08.010
I was like, no, he saved me

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.289
because I was about to be a stripper.

00:01:10.289 --> 00:01:14.300
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.466
- Making money where you can.

00:01:15.466 --> 00:01:16.440
- You got to do what you got to do.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.910
- Well, we have a house full
of single moms and dads,

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:20.750
and a few of them would love to share

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.630
what they're going through
so we can weigh in.

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:23.940
I don't know if you want me to weigh in,

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:24.950
but let's get to it.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:26.540
So where's Deseret?

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:27.373
- Right here.

00:01:27.373 --> 00:01:28.206
- Hi Deseret.

00:01:28.206 --> 00:01:29.039
- Hi.
(audience applauding)

00:01:29.039 --> 00:01:30.387
Hi Kelly, nice to meet you.

00:01:30.387 --> 00:01:31.350
- [Kelly] Hi.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:36.350
- I have two kids and I've been
a single mom since day one.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.170
They're amazing children,

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:41.840
but my brother always tells
me that I reward bad behavior.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.620
For example, if we're at a store

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.180
and they're like fussing around

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.410
and they tell me to buy them something

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:49.690
and I just kind of give
in and buy it for them

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:52.280
'cause I just don't want
to deal with it anymore.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:54.090
And I feel like I'm too soft

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.780
and I have a hard time disciplining them.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:57.790
And I just...

00:01:57.790 --> 00:01:59.653
- We're so different Deseret.

00:02:01.629 --> 00:02:02.462
- Oh my God.

00:02:02.462 --> 00:02:04.630
- They're about to be
pre-teen so I need help,

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:06.400
like breaking this cycle

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.450
and bringing some balance back to my life.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:09.938
- Oh my God, that cycle is going.

00:02:09.938 --> 00:02:11.175
- It's gone.

00:02:11.175 --> 00:02:12.205
The cycle is gone.

00:02:12.205 --> 00:02:13.038
- They are taking advantage of me.

00:02:13.038 --> 00:02:14.250
- Here's the thing

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.560
I will relate to and
I think everybody can,

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:18.620
sometimes they just wear you down.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:19.453
You're just like,

00:02:19.453 --> 00:02:21.880
I'm just tired of having
this conversation.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:23.190
You're just, you're exhausted.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:25.290
You're like, I cannot
believe you're surprised

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:27.070
that bedtime happens every night.

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:30.020
Like, why are we having this argument?

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:30.853
And it wears you down.

00:02:30.853 --> 00:02:32.240
So I get why you kind of give in,

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:34.020
but I will tell you what.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.770
Literally my kids the other day,

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:36.900
they were fighting over something

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:38.800
'cause they do that thing where,

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:39.633
there's is a little different.

00:02:39.633 --> 00:02:41.580
Like they know that if we go to a store,

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:42.413
I prep them.

00:02:42.413 --> 00:02:43.920
I say, we're going in this store

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.060
and you're not getting anything.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.150
We're doing something for
somebody else or whatever.

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:48.910
Or I prep them and say, hey,

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:50.530
if y'all want to grab
something like little,

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:51.940
you get one little thing or something,

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:55.180
but I am big on prepping
them because if you don't,

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:56.920
that's when the nightmare happens.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:00.210
And also they were fighting
the other day over something

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:01.160
and they were so entitled.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.240
I mean, y'all have so many toys.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:05.950
And so I took that toy
straight to the trash.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:07.500
- That's what I'm talking about.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:08.880
- I was like, I'm sorry.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.870
Since neither one of you
knows how to share it,

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.983
we will give it to the garbage.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:15.163
And it's gone.

00:03:15.163 --> 00:03:17.200
- Until they go in the
garbage and get it out.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.310
- Oh, they won't go in the garbage.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:19.830
They hate that I make
them take the trash out.

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:21.270
- Oh, God.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:23.350
Joshua has pulled out many
toys from the garbage.

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:24.183
- Oh, really?

00:03:24.183 --> 00:03:26.160
- I threw his iPad away one day,

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.027
oh, I went and got that out.

00:03:28.027 --> 00:03:30.969
(audience laughing)

00:03:30.969 --> 00:03:32.360
But I had to teach him a lesson.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:34.343
He was crying, oh my God, oh my God.

00:03:34.343 --> 00:03:36.130
As soon as he went to bed, I was like,

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:37.630
don't let me forget that iPad.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.280
- That was $700.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.113
- Exactly.

00:03:42.064 --> 00:03:44.750
But you have to, I think,
you know, especially,

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:46.600
I mean, they're preteen.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.050
You haven't missed the window,

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:50.040
but now you're gonna have
to probably attack it

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.710
a little differently because
I had the same problem,

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:55.030
but you have to start
as early as possible.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:57.870
For anyone else that is
listening, you know that,

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.810
especially if they go in a store,

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:02.420
for people with kids that have a tantrum,

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:04.920
my child has had a tantrum in the store

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.483
and I had one right with him.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:08.807
- Everybody has,

00:04:10.152 --> 00:04:14.300
that's like when we go to
Disneyland and you see,

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.370
like Disney, I feel like theme parks

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:19.180
are the place you see
most families just broken

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:20.300
on the ground.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.390
Like this is supposed to
be the happiest place ever

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:24.836
and they're just like God, I wanna leave.

00:04:24.836 --> 00:04:26.770
Like everybody in here just like,

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:29.100
oh, I feel at home,
everybody's the same army.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:29.933
- It's so funny.

00:04:29.933 --> 00:04:31.337
And I love when you see
the parents just walking

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:32.914
and the kids are screaming behind them.

00:04:32.914 --> 00:04:35.040
(Kym imitating a crying child)

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.150
And the parents are just walking.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:36.983
So what do you want to eat?

00:04:36.983 --> 00:04:37.818
I don't know.

00:04:37.818 --> 00:04:39.676
(audience applauding)

00:04:39.676 --> 00:04:40.509
- That's a good one though.

00:04:40.509 --> 00:04:42.232
We all have problems.

00:04:42.232 --> 00:04:43.232
- Thank you.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.020
- Where's Tony?

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:47.113
Hi Tony.
- Right here.

00:04:47.113 --> 00:04:50.113
(audience clapping)

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:52.510
Hi Kelly.

00:04:52.510 --> 00:04:55.710
I'm a single dad of a 13 year old daughter

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:57.170
and she is amazing.

00:04:57.170 --> 00:04:58.703
I love her to death.

00:04:58.703 --> 00:05:02.010
When she was younger, our
relationship was awesome.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.370
We did everything together,

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:06.670
vacations cruises,
homework time, everything.

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:09.410
She was a daddy's girl, 100% daddy's girl,

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:11.020
but she's a teenager now.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:12.610
And things are getting a little tricky.

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:16.050
And I have been a single
dad for five years now.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:17.250
And I mean, single, single,

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:20.080
like not even one date in five years.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:22.660
And yeah, exactly.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:23.710
But I'm ready now.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.950
I think I'm ready to start dating again.

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:27.350
- Oh, to have the
conversation with her now?

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:30.040
- Yes and so that's what I'm here for.

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:32.060
I want her to know that she's still

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:35.510
the number one girl in my
life and will always be,

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:38.760
but how do I go about
having that conversation

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:42.172
where daddy's on Bumble now.

00:05:42.172 --> 00:05:45.172
(audience laughing)

00:05:46.392 --> 00:05:47.602
- Daddy's on Bumble.

00:05:47.602 --> 00:05:48.543
- I love that.

00:05:48.543 --> 00:05:49.757
(audience clapping)

00:05:49.757 --> 00:05:51.137
- That's hard.

00:05:51.137 --> 00:05:51.970
How do you do that?

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:53.710
- Tony's tripping, Tony's tripping.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:56.070
So Tony look, what's your daughter's name?

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:56.903
- Ava.

00:05:56.903 --> 00:05:59.243
- Get Ava tonight, bring her over.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:02.745
We're gonna go to dinner,
Ava's gonna be with me.

00:06:02.745 --> 00:06:04.770
You're gonna be like, this is Kym,

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:06.930
we're just going out to dinner.

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:09.900
I'm gonna reach over and
rub your hand a little bit.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:11.186
She's gonna freak out.

00:06:11.186 --> 00:06:14.353
(audience applauding)

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:19.110
- I'm holding you to that.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:19.950
I'm holding you to that.

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:21.230
- Oh my God.

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:24.383
- I feel like I gotta do
some charity, five years.

00:06:25.217 --> 00:06:26.050
I got you.

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:27.633
- Five years.

00:06:27.633 --> 00:06:28.571
- Five years.

00:06:28.571 --> 00:06:29.910
- Oh my God.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.000
- I got to tell you though, I don't know,

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:32.950
I feel like that's,

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:37.050
I'm still where you were years ago.

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:39.380
So I don't have to worry about that yet,

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:42.730
but I feel like as long
as you still show her

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:44.650
that she's, you know, with your actions,

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.300
that she's still number one priority.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.330
I think that's the thing, right?

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:50.250
But she's got to know
that you have a life,

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:51.100
like she's got to know that you...

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:53.870
- You know Ava is in her room at night,

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:55.590
hey, is your mother single?

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:58.334
Somebody get my daddy a girlfriend.

00:06:58.334 --> 00:06:59.570
Are you kidding me?

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:01.727
- Not all kids.

00:07:01.727 --> 00:07:03.780
Some kids get freaked out.

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:07.310
- But that's why he has to
start bringing women around.

00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:08.500
- Well, not a lot.

00:07:10.331 --> 00:07:11.670
- I don't know these days.

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:15.180
Just bring a man or woman,
somebody around, okay,

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:17.940
that you're dating or who
want to date a potential

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:21.780
because they have to see the
interaction that it eases in.

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:24.320
Because I learned this from Nia Long,

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:25.730
because I had an argument with her

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:28.360
when my son was first born,

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:30.450
she was saying that you should introduce

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.000
the person you're dating early.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.680
And I said, no, absolutely not.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:36.210
I have to wait until he's older

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:38.020
and then I'll bring them
around once I know (indistinct)

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:41.730
She said, no, you bring them
around as friends first.

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:43.300
So it won't be foreign.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:45.010
I saw her the other night,
we're doing a movie together.

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:47.140
And I saw her and I apologized.

00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:48.800
I started a little Twitter argument.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.420
I said, you were absolutely right.

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:53.820
So what I do is bring
men around with my son,

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:56.430
introduced as a friend
so there's, you know,

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:59.410
he just sees that, you know,
mommy has male friends.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:02.400
Now I can tell if we're gonna go further,

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:05.330
then maybe we'll do some
family things together

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:08.350
and it'll go deeper and it
won't be a surprise to him.

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:11.870
Also, kids are very
good at seeing red flags

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:14.472
because my child would say,
mommy, you know he smokes weed.

00:08:14.472 --> 00:08:17.472
(audience laughing)

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:23.805
- Please tell me your
response is, so does mommy.

00:08:23.805 --> 00:08:26.490
(audience laughing)

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:27.818
- Oh my God.

00:08:27.818 --> 00:08:28.997
I can't take you.

00:08:31.404 --> 00:08:32.986
- That would be the greatest response.

00:08:32.986 --> 00:08:34.467
- Could you imagine.

00:08:34.467 --> 00:08:35.783
And so does mommy.

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:38.316
- It's gonna be all right.

00:08:38.316 --> 00:08:39.190
- Oh, that would be horrible.

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:40.300
- Oh my God.
- Oh my God.

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:41.280
- That's a hard one though.

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:42.113
That is a hard one.

00:08:42.113 --> 00:08:44.060
But I think five years, you've
put in enough time, man.

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:45.280
It's your turn.

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:46.254
It's your turn.

00:08:46.254 --> 00:08:47.500
(audience clapping)

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:48.880
Thanks Tony, good luck.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.534
Let's move on to Johara.

00:08:50.534 --> 00:08:52.343
(audience clapping)

00:08:52.343 --> 00:08:53.176
Hi Johara.

00:08:54.174 --> 00:08:55.760
- How's it going?

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.323
- What a cool name first of all.

00:08:57.323 --> 00:08:58.360
- Appreciate it, appreciate it.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:01.380
- Yeah, so what's going on
in your single parent world?

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:05.340
- So I am a single dad to
a beautiful and creative,

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:07.430
nearly 10 year old, right?

00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:09.340
Sometimes she'll spend
time with me out here,

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:12.390
but she lives in Louisiana
with her mom and her family.

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:15.210
But I do my best to keep
in contact with her,

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:18.630
call her on the phone, FaceTime
her and things like that.

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:20.740
So now she's at the age where,

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.070
puberty is starting to hit

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:23.810
and I'm kinda not ready for that.

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:25.490
- Yeah, good luck, yeah.

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:28.400
- So I want to have that
conversation with her,

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:30.320
but you know, it's kind of awkward.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:33.060
How do I go about having
that conversation with her

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:34.810
without making it weird?

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:35.760
- Oh, wow.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:38.160
First of all, next time she comes out,

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:39.503
I got a 10 year old too.

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:42.023
I'm just saying.

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:45.696
I mean, you're single, I'm single.

00:09:45.696 --> 00:09:48.696
(audience laughing)

00:09:50.001 --> 00:09:50.834
Hey, I'm just trying to help the cause.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:54.970
For me, I felt like this,

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:58.400
my mom and dad gave me a book.

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:01.566
I'm telling you, they gave me
a book and said, good luck.

00:10:01.566 --> 00:10:02.399
- Oh my gosh.

00:10:02.399 --> 00:10:03.830
- Yeah, that was at the time that parents

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:07.200
were pretty nervous about
talking about the birds and bees.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:09.030
I don't know about you,
they weren't comfortable.

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:09.863
But let me tell you something,

00:10:09.863 --> 00:10:12.620
if she's 10 years old, we got
Instagram, we got Facebook.

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:15.600
We got all these, your
